From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: KYTY_FSR upscales smaller game frames with AMD FSR 1

With KYTY_FSR set, a game frame that is smaller than the screen (a game told
the TV is 1080p, on a 4K TV) is drawn with FSR 1 EASU, the edge-adaptive
upscaler, instead of a linear blit. SDR frames only; HDR frames and frames that
are not upscaled keep the blit.
